<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="SINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_SrcQ" DataType="SINT" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Register for building Source / Quality enumeration]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="SINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Off-Scan: no Val update or alarm checking.  PV Bad Qualtiy ("stale") is asserted.]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
If this device is OFF-SCAN (rung is false or EnableIn is false in FBD), then:

Handle "NO MODE" Selection using the standard P_Mode AOI (EnableInFalse Routine, false scan required!).

NOTE:  IN ORDER TO AVOID USING AN "AFI" (which will generate a routine verify warning),
THIS RUNG USES AN XIC of Cfg_PCmdClear, followed by an XIO of the SAME BIT
to ensure P_Mode is SCANNED FALSE ("NO MODE").

THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE AND MUST APPEAR EXACTLY AS SHOWN FOR PROPER OPERATION!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration still needs to happen, even when device is disabled.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung publishes the Values for the scaled range.
If this instruction is reverse scaled by reversing the scaled (EU) min and max configurations,
the values are swapped so the the EUMax Value is always greater than the EUMin Value.
This makes the HMI bargraph and trend coding easier, and provides values
that can be pinned to the configuration of a PID, so the AIn and PID ranges are in lockstep.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GEQ(Cfg_PVEUMax,Cfg_PVEUMin) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVEUMin) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMax,Val_PVEUMax) ,LES(Cfg_PVEUMax,Cfg_PVEUMin) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVEUMax) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMax,Val_PVEUMin) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles the reports of all Bad Configuration Status.
Individual bits are provided for various status:
Bad Raw Scaling configs
Bad Engineering Units Scaling configs
Bad 1st-Order Filter configs
Bad Cfg_HasPVx configs (at least one must be set)
Bad Cfg_UsePVx configs (at least one must be set)

Since this Analog Input is disabled, indicate that the PV is bad
(Val is not being updated.)
Indicate that this Analog Input is DISABLED (Val_Sts = 33);
if there is a Configuration Error, indicate that as well (Val_Fault=34).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Sts_MaintByp) OTL(Sts_PVBad) ,CLR(Wrk_Fault) ,[EQU(Cfg_InpRawMax,Cfg_InpRawMin) OTE(Err_Raw) ,EQU(Cfg_PVEUMax,Cfg_PVEUMin) OTE(Err_EU) ,LES(Cfg_FiltTC,0.0) OTE(Err_Filt) ,LIM(9,Cfg_MinGood,0) OTE(Err_MinGood) ,XIO(Cfg_HasPVA) XIO(Cfg_HasPVB) XIO(Cfg_HasPVC) XIO(Cfg_HasPVD) XIO(Cfg_HasPVE) XIO(Cfg_HasPVF) XIO(Cfg_HasPVG) XIO(Cfg_HasPVH) OTE(Err_Has) ,XIO(Err_Has) XIO(Cfg_UsePVA) XIO(Cfg_UsePVB) XIO(Cfg_UsePVC) XIO(Cfg_UsePVD) XIO(Cfg_UsePVE) XIO(Cfg_UsePVF) XIO(Cfg_UsePVG) XIO(Cfg_UsePVH) OTE(Err_Use) ] OTE(Sts_Err) MOV(34,Wrk_Fault) ,MOV(33,Val_Sts) MOV(Wrk_Fault,Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ANALOG INPUT PROCESSING
============================================================
These rungs check the bit patterns of the REAL inputs (by copying to a pair of DINTs)
to see if each input is +Infinity, -Infinity or Not a Number.  Per ANSI 32-bit Float
format, in these cases the Exponent bits (.30 thru .23) will all be 1s:
0111 1111 1000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 = +Infinity
1111 1111 1000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 = -Infinity
x111 1111 1xxx xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx = Not a Number

If NOT in Simulation, copy each of the live PVs configured to exist.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVA,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVA,Val_PVA,1) COP(Set_SimPVA,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpAInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVB,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVB,Val_PVB,1) COP(Set_SimPVB,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpBInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVC,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVC,Val_PVC,1) COP(Set_SimPVC,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpCInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVD,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVD,Val_PVD,1) COP(Set_SimPVD,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpDInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVE,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVE,Val_PVE,1) COP(Set_SimPVE,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpEInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVF,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVF,Val_PVF,1) COP(Set_SimPVF,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpFInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVG,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVG,Val_PVG,1) COP(Set_SimPVG,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpGInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVH,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVH,Val_PVH,1) COP(Set_SimPVH,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpHInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If this object is NOT in simulation and the scaling constants are Valid (min not equal max),
scale each PV that is NOT infinite or NaN (not a number) to engineering units.

A proportionality value is calculated [  (EUMax-EUMin)/(RawMax-RawMin)  ] once and
used 8 times to avoid repeating the same floating point sub / sub / divide over and over
(reduce scan time a bit).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)XIO(Err_Raw)XIO(Err_EU)[CPT(Wrk_Scale,(Cfg_PVEUMax-Cfg_PVEUMin)/(Cfg_InpRawMax-Cfg_InpRawMin)) ,XIO(Wrk_InpAInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVA,(Inp_PVA-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpBInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVB,(Inp_PVB-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpCInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVC,(Inp_PVC-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpDInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVD,(Inp_PVD-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpEInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVE,(Inp_PVE-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpFInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVF,(Inp_PVF-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpGInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVG,(Inp_PVG-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpHInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVH,(Inp_PVH-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If scaling constants are NOT valid (Max = Min), then just set the
PVs to the minimum scaled EU value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ][MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVA) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVB) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVC) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVD) ,MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVE) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVF) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVG) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVH) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If NOT in simulation, if an input is INFINITE or NOT A NUMBER,
copy it (without scaling) to the PV to preserve the (Inf, NaN) bit pattern.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Wrk_InpAInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVA,Val_PVA,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpBInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVB,Val_PVB,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpCInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVC,Val_PVC,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpDInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVD,Val_PVD,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpEInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVE,Val_PVE,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpFInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVF,Val_PVF,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpGInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVG,Val_PVG,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpHInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVH,Val_PVH,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If this object is NOT in simulation and the scaling constants are Valid (min not equal max),
scale each PV that is NOT INFINITE or NOT A NUMBER to engineering units.

A proportionality value is calculated [  (EUMax-EUMin)/(RawMax-RawMin)  ] once and
used 8 times to avoid repeating the same floating point sub / sub / divide over and over
(reduce scan time a bit).

The Raw Inputs are scaled to Engineering Units if selected to exist
and scaling constants are valid.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)XIO(Err_Raw)XIO(Err_EU)[CPT(Wrk_Scale,(Cfg_PVEUMax-Cfg_PVEUMin)/(Cfg_InpRawMax-Cfg_InpRawMin)) ,XIO(Wrk_InpAInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVA,(Inp_PVA-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpBInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVB,(Inp_PVB-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpCInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVC,(Inp_PVC-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpDInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVD,(Inp_PVD-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpEInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVE,(Inp_PVE-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpFInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVF,(Inp_PVF-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpGInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVG,(Inp_PVG-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpHInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVH,(Inp_PVH-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If scaling constants are NOT valid (Max = Min), then just set the
PVs to the minimum scaled EU value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ][MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVA) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVB) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVC) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVD) ,MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVE) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVF) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVG) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVH) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If NOT in simulation, if an input is INFINITE or NOT A NUMBER,
copy it (without scaling) to the PV to preserve the (Inf, NaN) bit pattern.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Wrk_InpAInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVA,Val_PVA,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpBInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVB,Val_PVB,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpCInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVC,Val_PVC,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpDInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVD,Val_PVD,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpEInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVE,Val_PVE,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpFInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVF,Val_PVF,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpGInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVG,Val_PVG,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpHInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVH,Val_PVH,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When this Analog Input is not simulated, and if tracking is enabled,
the Simulated PV Settings track the Input PVs for bumpless transfer into Simulation.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)XIC(Cfg_SetTrack)[COP(Val_PVA,Set_SimPVA,1) COP(Val_PVB,Set_SimPVB,1) COP(Val_PVC,Set_SimPVC,1) COP(Val_PVD,Set_SimPVD,1) ,COP(Val_PVE,Set_SimPVE,1) COP(Val_PVF,Set_SimPVF,1) COP(Val_PVG,Set_SimPVG,1) COP(Val_PVH,Set_SimPVH,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SELECTED PV CHECK
============================================================
This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVA,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVAInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SENSOR OUT OF RANGE DETECTION
============================================================
The following rungs check each sensor for Out of Range condition

If the Sensor A Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor A as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVA)XIO(Wrk_SelPVAInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVA,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVA,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVAOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVA>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVA<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVAOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVB,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVBInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Sensor B Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor B as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVB)XIO(Wrk_SelPVBInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVB,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVB,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVBOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVB>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVB<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVBOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVC,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVCInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Sensor C Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor C as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVC)XIO(Wrk_SelPVCInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVC,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVC,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVCOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVC>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVC<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVCOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVD,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVDInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Sensor D Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor D as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVD)XIO(Wrk_SelPVDInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVD,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVD,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVDOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVD>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVD<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVDOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVE,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVEInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Sensor E Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor E as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVE)XIO(Wrk_SelPVEInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVE,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVE,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVEOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVE>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVE<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVEOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVF,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVFInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Sensor F Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor F as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVF)XIO(Wrk_SelPVFInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVF,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVF,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVFOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVF>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVF<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVFOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVG,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVGInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Sensor G Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor G as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVG)XIO(Wrk_SelPVGInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVG,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVG,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVGOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVG>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVG<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVGOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVH,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVHInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Sensor H Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor H as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVH)XIO(Wrk_SelPVHInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVH,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVH,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVHOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVH>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVH<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVHOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SENSOR REJECT LOGIC
============================================================
The following rungs determine which sensors to use in calculating the PV.
To start, ALL sensors are used (none are marked rejected).
The rungs below will mark off any sensors as "rejected" that should not be used
in computing the final PV.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Wrk_RejectedPVs)OTU(AnyReject.Inp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV A sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasPVA) OTU(Cfg_UsePVA) ,XIO(Cfg_UsePVA) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVA) [XIC(Wrk_PVAOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_InpAInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVABad) ,XIC(Inp_PVAUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(AnyReject.Inp) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV B sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasPVB) OTU(Cfg_UsePVB) ,XIO(Cfg_UsePVB) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVB) [XIC(Wrk_PVBOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_InpBInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVBBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVBUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(AnyReject.Inp) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV C sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasPVC) OTU(Cfg_UsePVC) ,XIO(Cfg_UsePVC) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVC) [XIC(Wrk_PVCOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_InpCInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVCBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVCUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(AnyReject.Inp) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV D sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasPVD) OTU(Cfg_UsePVD) ,XIO(Cfg_UsePVD) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVD) [XIC(Wrk_PVDOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_InpDInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVDBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVDUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(AnyReject.Inp) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV E sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasPVE) OTU(Cfg_UsePVE) ,XIO(Cfg_UsePVE) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVE) [XIC(Wrk_PVEOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_InpEInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVEBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVEUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(AnyReject.Inp) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.4);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV F sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasPVF) OTU(Cfg_UsePVF) ,XIO(Cfg_UsePVF) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVF) [XIC(Wrk_PVFOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_InpFInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVFBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVFUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(AnyReject.Inp) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.5);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV G sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasPVG) OTU(Cfg_UsePVG) ,XIO(Cfg_UsePVG) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVG) [XIC(Wrk_PVGOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_InpGInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVGBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVGUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(AnyReject.Inp) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.6);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV H sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasPVH) OTU(Cfg_UsePVH) ,XIO(Cfg_UsePVH) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVH) [XIC(Wrk_PVHOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_InpHInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVHBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVHUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(AnyReject.Inp) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.7);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SENSOR AVERAGE / MEDIAN LOGIC
============================================================
The following rungs determine how many good sensors there are and load
their PV values in an array for computing Standard Deviation and Average.

Start by clearing the count of good sensors.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Recalc)CLR(Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV A sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.0)MOV(Val_PVA,Wrk_GoodPVs[0])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV B sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.1)MOV(Val_PVB,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV C sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.2)MOV(Val_PVC,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="48" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV D sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.3)MOV(Val_PVD,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="49" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV E sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.4)MOV(Val_PVE,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="50" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV F sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.5)MOV(Val_PVF,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="51" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV G sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.6)MOV(Val_PVG,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="52" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV H sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.7)MOV(Val_PVH,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="53" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If there are less than two good sensors, we can't compute a standard deviation.  Skip the
average and standard deviation logic and just report the final sensor value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,1)JMP(Only1PV);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="54" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Next, see if any sensor is outside two standard deviations of the mean.

Start by computing the mean and standard deviation of the good sensors.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[RES(Wrk_StdCtrl) MOV(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_StdCtrl.LEN) STD(Wrk_GoodPVs[0],0,Wrk_Std,Wrk_StdCtrl,?,?) ,RES(Wrk_AvgCtrl) MOV(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_AvgCtrl.LEN) AVE(Wrk_GoodPVs[0],0,Wrk_Avg,Wrk_AvgCtrl,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="55" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For the MEDIAN of three or more PVs, we need the sorted set of good
PV values.  The Median is the "middle" value.

For an ODD number of good PVs, it's the central value.
For an EVEN number of good PVs, it's the average of the TWO central values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[RES(Wrk_SortCtrl)MOV(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_SortCtrl.LEN)SRT(Wrk_GoodPVs[0],0,Wrk_SortCtrl,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="56" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Now calculate the Median of the good PVs.  If there are TWO valid PVs,
the median is the average of the two good PVs.  No need to sort.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,2)CPT(Wrk_Median,(Wrk_GoodPVs[0]+Wrk_GoodPVs[1])/2.0)JMP(Only2PVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="57" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an ODD number of good PVs, the median is the central value from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,3)MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[1],Wrk_Median)JMP(DoDeviation);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="58" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an EVEN number of good PVs, the median is the average of the TWO central values
from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4)CPT(Wrk_Median,(Wrk_GoodPVs[1]+Wrk_GoodPVs[2])/2.0)JMP(DoDeviation);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="59" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an ODD number of good PVs, the median is the central value from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,5)MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[2],Wrk_Median)JMP(DoDeviation);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="60" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an EVEN number of good PVs, the median is the average of the TWO central values
from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,6)CPT(Wrk_Median,(Wrk_GoodPVs[2]+Wrk_GoodPVs[3])/2.0)JMP(DoDeviation);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="61" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an ODD number of good PVs, the median is the central value from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,7)MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[3],Wrk_Median)JMP(DoDeviation);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="62" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an EVEN number of good PVs, the median is the average of the TWO central values
from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,8)CPT(Wrk_Median,(Wrk_GoodPVs[3]+Wrk_GoodPVs[4])/2.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="63" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute "mean plus 2 SDs" and "mean minus 2 SDs"
for use in checking individual sensors.  (This avoids recomputing these
values in multple CMP instructions, saving scan time.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(DoDeviation)OTU(Wrk_RejectDev)CPT(Wrk_Plus2Std,Wrk_Avg+2.0*Wrk_Std)CPT(Wrk_Minus2Std,Wrk_Avg-2.0*Wrk_Std)CLR(Wrk_WorstDev)CLR(Wrk_WorstPtr);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="64" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV A sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.0)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVA,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVA,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVA-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVA-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVA-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [CLR(Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="65" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV B sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.1)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVB,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVB,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVB-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVB-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVB-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(1,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="66" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV C sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.2)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVC,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVC,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVC-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVC-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVC-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(2,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="67" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV D sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.3)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVD,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVD,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVD-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVD-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVD-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(3,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="68" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV E sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.4)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVE,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVE,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVE-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVE-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVE-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(4,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="69" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV F sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.5)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVF,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVF,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVF-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVF-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVF-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(5,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="70" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV G sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.6)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVG,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVG,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVG-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVG-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVG-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(6,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="71" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV H sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.7)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVH,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVH,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVH-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVH-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVH-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(7,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="72" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY sensor was rejected for being outside 2 standard deviations
from the mean, go back and recompute the mean and stadard devaition
of the remaining "good" sensors.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_RejectDev)OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.[Wrk_WorstPtr])OTL(AnyReject.Inp)JMP(Recalc);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="73" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SELECT FINAL MEAN OR MEDIAN
============================================================
If there are NO valid (unrejected) sensors, set the PV to NOT A NUMBER.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Only1PV)EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,0)MOV(16#7F80_0001,Wrk_CalcPVDINT)COP(Wrk_CalcPVDINT,Wrk_PV,1)JMP(SelSubst);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="74" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If there is ONLY ONE valid PV, it is the final value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,1)MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[0],Wrk_PV)JMP(SelSubst);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="75" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Special Case:  If there are exactly two good PVs, select the PV value from
the sorted input list based on the configuration Cfg_CalcWhen2:
0 = select average of the two input,
1 = select minimum (first element in sorted list),
2 = select maximum (second element in sorted list)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Only2PVs)EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,2)[MOV(Wrk_Median,Wrk_PV) ,EQU(Cfg_CalcWhen2,1) MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[0],Wrk_PV) ,EQU(Cfg_CalcWhen2,2) MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[1],Wrk_PV) ]JMP(SelSubst);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="76" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If there are THREE OR MORE valid PVs, use the already-computed
average or median of the good PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) MOV(Wrk_Avg,Wrk_PV) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) MOV(Wrk_Median,Wrk_PV) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="77" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Here's the PV calculated.  Remember, in EnableInFalse, we don't update Val (the value)
or allow selection of substitute PV.  But we do update the calculated PV based on inputs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SelSubst)MOV(Wrk_PV,Val_CalcPV);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="78" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If any PV that's enabled has been rejected for any reason,
flag that PV with a Rejected Status bit.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_UsePVA) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.0) OTE(Sts_PVAReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVB) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.1) OTE(Sts_PVBReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVC) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.2) OTE(Sts_PVCReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVD) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.3) OTE(Sts_PVDReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVE) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.4) OTE(Sts_PVEReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVF) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.5) OTE(Sts_PVFReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVG) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.6) OTE(Sts_PVGReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVH) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.7) OTE(Sts_PVHReject) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="79" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED STATUS VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_PVA
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasChanObjA) MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQA) ,XIC(Cfg_HasChanObjA) MOV(Inp_PVASrcQ,Wrk_SrcQA) ,XIC(Inp_PVAUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQA) ,XIC(Inp_PVABad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQA) ,[XIC(Wrk_InpAInfNaN) ,XIC(Wrk_PVAOutOfRange) ] MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQA) ,[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ] MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQA) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQA) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQA,SrcQ_IOA) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="80" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_PVB
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasChanObjB) MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQB) ,XIC(Cfg_HasChanObjB) MOV(Inp_PVBSrcQ,Wrk_SrcQB) ,XIC(Inp_PVBUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQB) ,XIC(Inp_PVBBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQB) ,[XIC(Wrk_InpBInfNaN) ,XIC(Wrk_PVBOutOfRange) ] MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQB) ,[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ] MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQB) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQB) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQB,SrcQ_IOB) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="81" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_PVC
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
