34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasChanObjD) MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQD) ,XIC(Cfg_HasChanObjD) MOV(Inp_PVDSrcQ,Wrk_SrcQD) ,XIC(Inp_PVDUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQD) ,XIC(Inp_PVDBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQD) ,[XIC(Wrk_InpDInfNaN) ,XIC(Wrk_PVDOutOfRange) ] MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQD) ,[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ] MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQD) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQD) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQD,SrcQ_IOD) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="83" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_PVE
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasChanObjE) MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQE) ,XIC(Cfg_HasChanObjE) MOV(Inp_PVESrcQ,Wrk_SrcQE) ,XIC(Inp_PVEUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQE) ,XIC(Inp_PVEBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQE) ,[XIC(Wrk_InpEInfNaN) ,XIC(Wrk_PVEOutOfRange) ] MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQE) ,[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ] MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQE) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQE) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQE,SrcQ_IOE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="84" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_PVF
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasChanObjF) MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQF) ,XIC(Cfg_HasChanObjF) MOV(Inp_PVFSrcQ,Wrk_SrcQF) ,XIC(Inp_PVFUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQF) ,XIC(Inp_PVFBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQF) ,[XIC(Wrk_InpFInfNaN) ,XIC(Wrk_PVFOutOfRange) ] MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQF) ,[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ] MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQF) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQF) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQF,SrcQ_IOF) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="85" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_PVG
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasChanObjG) MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQG) ,XIC(Cfg_HasChanObjG) MOV(Inp_PVGSrcQ,Wrk_SrcQG) ,XIC(Inp_PVGUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQG) ,XIC(Inp_PVGBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQG) ,[XIC(Wrk_InpGInfNaN) ,XIC(Wrk_PVGOutOfRange) ] MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQG) ,[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ] MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQG) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQG) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQG,SrcQ_IOA) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="86" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_PVH
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasChanObjH) MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQH) ,XIC(Cfg_HasChanObjH) MOV(Inp_PVHSrcQ,Wrk_SrcQH) ,XIC(Inp_PVHUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQH) ,XIC(Inp_PVHBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQH) ,[XIC(Wrk_InpHInfNaN) ,XIC(Wrk_PVHOutOfRange) ] MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQH) ,[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ] MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQH) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQH) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQH,SrcQ_IOH) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="87" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality (SrcQ) for Val (primary value)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(19,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="88" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as the Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(MCmd_InpPV)OTU(MCmd_SubstPV)OTU(OCmd_Reset)OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll)OTU(PCmd_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="89" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Since we're not processing Operator Commands or Settings, we're not READY for any of them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Rdy_InpPV)OTU(Rdy_SubstPV)OTU(Rdy_Reset)OTU(Rdy_ResetAckAll)OTU(Rdy_OSet);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="90" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The first-order filter's scan timer must run and clear every scan, whether the Instruction
is true or not.  Doing so here avoids a bump in the Value on transition to EnableIn TRUE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[TON(Wrk_ScanT,?,?)CLR(Wrk_ScanT.ACC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="91" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Set up the filter initialization one-shot so filter of "Val" in main Logic
will start from first valid value on transition from false to true.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_ValidONS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="92" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Alarms and the Notify Status, and show the Alarms Inhibited breadcrumb.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Alm_HiHi) OTU(Alm_Hi) OTU(Alm_Lo) OTU(Alm_LoLo) ,OTU(Alm_AnyReject) OTU(Alm_MinGood) OTU(Alm_Fail) ,OTU(Sts_HiHi) OTU(Sts_Hi) OTU(Sts_Lo) OTU(Sts_LoLo) ,OTU(Sts_AnyReject) OTU(Sts_MinGood) OTU(Sts_Fail) ,OTL(Sts_AlmInh) CLR(Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Normal Scan - Inputs scaled, average or median PV calculated, alarms generated]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_AInMulti:  PROCESS -- MULTIPLE (to 8) ANALOG INPUT
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Uses P_Gate, P_AIChan, P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.0.
Added Inf_Lib.
V3.0-01  2013-07-30:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-02  2013-09-03:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-03  2013-10-30:  Corrected Parameter descriptions and default
configuration values for alarms only.
V3.0-04  2014-5-12:   Improved handling of Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.
V3.1-00  2014-07-18:  Modified to use P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1, add SrcQ enums.
Modified to consistently use alias tag names.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Inp_PVSrcQ pulled into all bad/uncertain logic.
Using P_Alarm, P_Gate, P_Mode V3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This Instruction monitors an Analog Input from multiple flow, level, pressure,
pH, dissolved oxygen, temperature, or any other analog sensors, and provides:

*  Scaling, from Input (Raw) to PV (Engineering) Units
*  High-High, High, Low and Low-Low Status and Alarms, with Gate
inputs and configurable on-delay, off-delay and gate delay times
*  Monitoring of input communication status and out-of-range conditions for each sensor
*  Calculation of a single PV based on the mean (average) or median (selectable) of good sensor values
*  Exclusion of Bad PVs, Uncertain PVs (configurable), out of range PVs, PVs excluded by Maintenance
*  Exclusion of PVs either outside two standard deviations from the mean (for at least 4 PV)
or ouside a user-configured deviation threshold from the mean (selectable) from the PV calculation
*  For the degenerate case where only 2 PVs remain, configuration determines whether the
higher, lower or average of the two good PVs is used.
*  Setting of a simulated signal for each input for process simulation
*  Program and Operator Settings for Alarm Thresholds
*  Maintenance Commands to allow manual override of the calculated PV (Substitute PV)
*  Capturing of the lowest and highest PV excursion values

Modes are provided by a P_Mode AOI instance.
Alarms are provided by P_Alarm AOI instances.
Status gating provided by P_Gate AOI instances.
Modes of operation: Operator, Program, Maintenance
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Cfg_PVATag,Cfg_PVBTag)LOWER(Cfg_PVCTag,Cfg_PVDTag)LOWER(Cfg_PVETag,Cfg_PVFTag)LOWER(Cfg_PVGTag,Cfg_PVHTag)CONCAT(Cfg_EU,Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MODE PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Mode Inputs and Commands:

NOTE:  All Commands for Mode, Alarm are aliased directly to the
corresponding Commands in the contained P_Mode and P_Alarm AOIs.

This object does NOT have the following Modes:
Hand
Override]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)OTU(Mode.Inp_Hand)OTU(Mode.Inp_Ovrd)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles simple First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung publishes the Values for the scaled range.
If this instruction is reverse scaled by reversing the scaled (EU) min and max configurations,
the values are swapped so the the EUMax Value is always greater than the EUMin Value.
This makes the HMI bargraph and trend coding easier, and provides values
that can be pinned to the configuration of a PID, so the AIn and PID ranges are in lockstep.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GEQ(Cfg_PVEUMax,Cfg_PVEUMin) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVEUMin) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMax,Val_PVEUMax) ,LES(Cfg_PVEUMax,Cfg_PVEUMin) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVEUMax) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMax,Val_PVEUMin) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If this instruction is configured not to HAVE a particular PV,
it cannot USE that PV!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(8,Wrk_NumInputs) ,XIO(Cfg_HasPVA) OTU(Cfg_UsePVA) SUB(Wrk_NumInputs,1,Wrk_NumInputs) ,XIO(Cfg_HasPVB) OTU(Cfg_UsePVB) SUB(Wrk_NumInputs,1,Wrk_NumInputs) ,XIO(Cfg_HasPVC) OTU(Cfg_UsePVC) SUB(Wrk_NumInputs,1,Wrk_NumInputs) ,XIO(Cfg_HasPVD) OTU(Cfg_UsePVD) SUB(Wrk_NumInputs,1,Wrk_NumInputs) ,XIO(Cfg_HasPVE) OTU(Cfg_UsePVE) SUB(Wrk_NumInputs,1,Wrk_NumInputs) ,XIO(Cfg_HasPVF) OTU(Cfg_UsePVF) SUB(Wrk_NumInputs,1,Wrk_NumInputs) ,XIO(Cfg_HasPVG) OTU(Cfg_UsePVG) SUB(Wrk_NumInputs,1,Wrk_NumInputs) ,XIO(Cfg_HasPVH) OTU(Cfg_UsePVH) SUB(Wrk_NumInputs,1,Wrk_NumInputs) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Flag a Configuration Error if the raw input range or scaled PV range
max and min are set the same (invalid range), or if the
Analog Input Filter Time Constant is set to a negative value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Cfg_InpRawMax,Cfg_InpRawMin) OTE(Err_Raw) ,EQU(Cfg_PVEUMax,Cfg_PVEUMin) OTE(Err_EU) ,LES(Cfg_FiltTC,0.0) OTE(Err_Filt) ,LIM(9,Cfg_MinGood,0) OTE(Err_MinGood) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SETTINGS PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Settings:

When the Mode is Program, use the Program Settings for the
Alarm Thresholds, and (if so enabled) copy the Program Settings to the Operator Settings
for bumpless transition from Program to Operator.

When the Mode is Operator, use the Operator Settings for the
Alarm Thresholds, and (if so enabled) copy the Operator Settings to the Program Settings
for bumpless transition from Operator to Program.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Prog) [MOV(PSet_HiHiLim,Val_HiHiLim) MOV(PSet_HiLim,Val_HiLim) MOV(PSet_LoLim,Val_LoLim) MOV(PSet_LoLoLim,Val_LoLoLim) ,XIC(Cfg_SetTrack) MOV(Val_HiHiLim,OSet_HiHiLim) MOV(Val_HiLim,OSet_HiLim) MOV(Val_LoLim,OSet_LoLim) MOV(Val_LoLoLim,OSet_LoLoLim) ] ,[XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] [MOV(OSet_HiHiLim,Val_HiHiLim) MOV(OSet_HiLim,Val_HiLim) MOV(OSet_LoLim,Val_LoLim) MOV(OSet_LoLoLim,Val_LoLoLim) ,XIC(Cfg_SetTrack) MOV(Val_HiHiLim,PSet_HiHiLim) MOV(Val_HiLim,PSet_HiLim) MOV(Val_LoLim,PSet_LoLim) MOV(Val_LoLoLim,PSet_LoLoLim) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready to receive other Operator Settings (OSet_xxx) if tracking is NOT enabled,
or we're in Operator or Maintenance Mode.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_SetTrack) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ]OTE(Rdy_OSet);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SUBSTITUTE PV / INPUT PV COMMAND PROCESSING
============================================================
These rungs handle the Substitute PV and Input PV Commands:

MCmd_SubstPV: Maintenance Command to select Maintenance-entered substitute PV

Do not allow this Command if Cfg_NoSubstPV is set.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_SubstPV)OTU(MCmd_SubstPV)XIC(Sts_Maint)XIO(Cfg_NoSubstPV)OTL(Wrk_SubstPV);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[MCmd_InpPV: Maintenance Command to cancel Substitute PV and return to Live Input PV.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(MCmd_InpPV) OTU(MCmd_InpPV) XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_NoSubstPV) ]OTU(Wrk_SubstPV);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the Substitute or Input PV Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_SubstPV) OTE(Sts_SubstPV) ,XIO(Wrk_SubstPV) OTE(Sts_InpPV) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Maintenance Bypass functions on this Analog Input include
choosing a Substitute PV, and marking a PV that Engineering says
this instruction HAS (is intended to use) as NOT USED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_SubstPV) ,XIC(Cfg_HasPVA) XIO(Cfg_UsePVA) ,XIC(Cfg_HasPVB) XIO(Cfg_UsePVB) ,XIC(Cfg_HasPVC) XIO(Cfg_UsePVC) ,XIC(Cfg_HasPVD) XIO(Cfg_UsePVD) ,XIC(Cfg_HasPVE) XIO(Cfg_UsePVE) ,XIC(Cfg_HasPVF) XIO(Cfg_UsePVF) ,XIC(Cfg_HasPVG) XIO(Cfg_UsePVG) ,XIC(Cfg_HasPVH) XIO(Cfg_UsePVH) ]OTE(Sts_MaintByp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[In Maintenance Mode, commands for Substitue PV and Input PV are available
based on the current state of the internal toggle bit.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Maint)XIO(Cfg_NoSubstPV)[XIO(Wrk_SubstPV) OTE(Rdy_SubstPV) ,XIC(Wrk_SubstPV) OTE(Rdy_InpPV) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Input and Commands
and the "Reset and Ack All" Operator Command.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) [OTL(PCmd_HiHiAck) OTL(PCmd_HiAck) ,OTL(PCmd_LoAck) OTL(PCmd_LoLoAck) ,OTL(PCmd_FailAck) OTL(PCmd_AnyRejectAck) ,OTL(PCmd_MinGoodAck) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ][OTL(HiHi.PCmd_Reset) OTL(Hi.PCmd_Reset) OTL(Lo.PCmd_Reset) OTL(LoLo.PCmd_Reset) ,OTL(Fail.PCmd_Reset) OTL(AnyReject.PCmd_Reset) OTL(MinGood.PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ANALOG INPUT PROCESSING
============================================================
These rungs check the bit patterns of the REAL inputs (by copying to a pair of DINTs)
to see if each input is +Infinity, -Infinity or Not a Number.  Per ANSI 32-bit Float
format, in these cases the Exponent bits (.30 thru .23) will all be 1s:
0111 1111 1000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 = +Infinity
1111 1111 1000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 = -Infinity
x111 1111 1xxx xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx = Not a Number

If NOT in Simulation, copy each of the live PVs configured to exist.
#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVA,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVA,Val_PVA,1) COP(Set_SimPVA,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpAInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVB,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVB,Val_PVB,1) COP(Set_SimPVB,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpBInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVC,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVC,Val_PVC,1) COP(Set_SimPVC,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpCInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVD,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVD,Val_PVD,1) COP(Set_SimPVD,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpDInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVE,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVE,Val_PVE,1) COP(Set_SimPVE,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpEInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVF,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVF,Val_PVF,1) COP(Set_SimPVF,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpFInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVG,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVG,Val_PVG,1) COP(Set_SimPVG,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpGInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) COP(Inp_PVH,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) COP(Set_SimPVH,Val_PVH,1) COP(Set_SimPVH,Wrk_InpPVDINT,1) ]MEQ(Wrk_InpPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_InpHInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If this object is NOT in simulation and the scaling constants are Valid (min not equal max),
scale each PV that is NOT infinite or NaN (not a number) to engineering units.

A proportionality value is calculated [  (EUMax-EUMin)/(RawMax-RawMin)  ] once and
used 8 times to avoid repeating the same floating point sub / sub / divide over and over
(reduce scan time a bit).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)XIO(Err_Raw)XIO(Err_EU)[CPT(Wrk_Scale,(Cfg_PVEUMax-Cfg_PVEUMin)/(Cfg_InpRawMax-Cfg_InpRawMin)) ,XIO(Wrk_InpAInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVA,(Inp_PVA-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpBInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVB,(Inp_PVB-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpCInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVC,(Inp_PVC-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpDInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVD,(Inp_PVD-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpEInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVE,(Inp_PVE-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpFInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVF,(Inp_PVF-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpGInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVG,(Inp_PVG-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ,XIO(Wrk_InpHInfNaN) CPT(Val_PVH,(Inp_PVH-Cfg_InpRawMin)*Wrk_Scale+Cfg_PVEUMin) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If scaling constants are NOT valid (Max = Min), then just set the
PVs to the minimum scaled EU value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ][MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVA) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVB) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVC) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVD) ,MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVE) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVF) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVG) MOV(Cfg_PVEUMin,Val_PVH) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If NOT in simulation, if an input is INFINITE or NOT A NUMBER,
copy it (without scaling) to the PV to preserve the (Inf, NaN) bit pattern.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Wrk_InpAInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVA,Val_PVA,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpBInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVB,Val_PVB,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpCInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVC,Val_PVC,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpDInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVD,Val_PVD,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpEInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVE,Val_PVE,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpFInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVF,Val_PVF,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpGInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVG,Val_PVG,1) ,XIC(Wrk_InpHInfNaN) COP(Inp_PVH,Val_PVH,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When this Analog Input is not simulated, and if tracking is enabled,
the Simulated PV Settings track the Input PVs for bumpless transfer into Simulation.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)XIC(Cfg_SetTrack)[COP(Val_PVA,Set_SimPVA,1) COP(Val_PVB,Set_SimPVB,1) COP(Val_PVC,Set_SimPVC,1) COP(Val_PVD,Set_SimPVD,1) ,COP(Val_PVE,Set_SimPVE,1) COP(Val_PVF,Set_SimPVF,1) COP(Val_PVG,Set_SimPVG,1) COP(Val_PVH,Set_SimPVH,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SELECTED PV CHECK
============================================================
This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVA,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVAInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SENSOR OUT OF RANGE DETECTION
============================================================
The following rungs check each sensor for Out of Range condition

If the Sensor A Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor A as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVA)XIO(Wrk_SelPVAInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVA,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVA,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVAOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVA>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVA<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVAOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVB,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVBInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Sensor B Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor B as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVB)XIO(Wrk_SelPVBInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVB,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVB,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVBOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVB>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVB<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVBOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVC,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVCInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Sensor C Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit, or falls below
the Fail Low Limit, has not come back within the limits (with deadband),
mark Sensor C as Out of Range.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVC)XIO(Wrk_SelPVCInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVC,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVC,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVCOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVC>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVC<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVCOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines whether the selected (Input, Simulated or Substitute)
Analog PV is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Val_PVD,Wrk_SelPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_SelPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SelPVDInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
