<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePVH)XIO(Wrk_SelPVHInfNaN)[GEQ(Val_PVH,Cfg_FailHiLim) ,LEQ(Val_PVH,Cfg_FailLoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_PVHOutOfRange) [CMP(Val_PVH>=(Cfg_FailHiLim-Cfg_FailDB)) ,CMP(Val_PVH<=(Cfg_FailLoLim+Cfg_FailDB)) ] ]OTE(Wrk_PVHOutOfRange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SENSOR REJECT LOGIC
============================================================
The following rungs determine which sensors to use in calculating the PV.
To start, ALL sensors are used (none are marked rejected).
The rungs below will mark off any sensors as "rejected" that should not be used
in computing the final PV.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Wrk_RejectedPVs)OTU(Wrk_AnyReject);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV A sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_UsePVA) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVA) [XIC(Wrk_PVAOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_SelPVAInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVABad) ,XIC(Inp_PVAUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(Wrk_AnyReject) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV B sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_UsePVB) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVB) [XIC(Wrk_PVBOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_SelPVBInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVBBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVBUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(Wrk_AnyReject) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV C sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_UsePVC) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVC) [XIC(Wrk_PVCOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_SelPVCInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVCBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVCUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(Wrk_AnyReject) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV D sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_UsePVD) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVD) [XIC(Wrk_PVDOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_SelPVDInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVDBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVDUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(Wrk_AnyReject) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV E sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_UsePVE) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVE) [XIC(Wrk_PVEOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_SelPVEInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVEBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVEUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(Wrk_AnyReject) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.4);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="48" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV F sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_UsePVF) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVF) [XIC(Wrk_PVFOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_SelPVFInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVFBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVFUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(Wrk_AnyReject) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.5);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="49" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV G sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_UsePVG) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVG) [XIC(Wrk_PVGOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_SelPVGInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVGBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVGUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(Wrk_AnyReject) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.6);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="50" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mark the PV H sensor "rejected" from the PV computation if:
* the sensor is not configured to exist, or
* Maintenance has configured the sensor to be ignored
Mark it "rejected" AND raise the Any Input Rejected Warning if the sensor is Used and:
* the sensor is out of range,
* the sensor input has "bad" quality,
* the sensor input has "uncertain" quality (if configured to reject uncertains),]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_UsePVH) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVH) [XIC(Wrk_PVHOutOfRange) ,XIC(Wrk_SelPVHInfNaN) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp_PVHBad) ,XIC(Inp_PVHUncertain) XIC(Cfg_RejectUncertain) ] ] OTL(Wrk_AnyReject) ]OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.7);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="51" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SENSOR AVERAGE / MEDIAN LOGIC
============================================================
The following rungs determine how many good sensors there are and load
their PV values in an array for computing Standard Deviation and Average.

Start by clearing the count of good sensors.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Recalc)CLR(Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="52" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV A sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.0)MOV(Val_PVA,Wrk_GoodPVs[0])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="53" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV B sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.1)MOV(Val_PVB,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="54" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV C sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.2)MOV(Val_PVC,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="55" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV D sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.3)MOV(Val_PVD,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="56" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV E sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.4)MOV(Val_PVE,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="57" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV F sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.5)MOV(Val_PVF,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="58" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV G sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.6)MOV(Val_PVG,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="59" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the PV H sensor is not rejected, load it in the computing array and add 1 to the "good" couont.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.7)MOV(Val_PVH,Wrk_GoodPVs[Wrk_NumGoodPVs])ADD(1,Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_NumGoodPVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="60" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If there are less than two good sensors, we can't compute a standard deviation.  Skip the
average and standard deviation logic and just report the final sensor value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,1)JMP(Only1PV);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="61" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Next, see if any sensor is outside two standard deviations of the mean.

Start by computing the mean and standard deviation of the good sensors.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[RES(Wrk_StdCtrl) MOV(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_StdCtrl.LEN) STD(Wrk_GoodPVs[0],0,Wrk_Std,Wrk_StdCtrl,?,?) ,RES(Wrk_AvgCtrl) MOV(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_AvgCtrl.LEN) AVE(Wrk_GoodPVs[0],0,Wrk_Avg,Wrk_AvgCtrl,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="62" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For the MEDIAN of three or more PVs, we need the sorted set of good
PV values.  The Median is the "middle" value.

For an ODD number of good PVs, it's the central value.
For an EVEN number of good PVs, it's the average of the TWO central values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[RES(Wrk_SortCtrl)MOV(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Wrk_SortCtrl.LEN)SRT(Wrk_GoodPVs[0],0,Wrk_SortCtrl,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="63" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Now calculate the Median of the good PVs.  If there are TWO valid PVs,
the median is the average of the two good PVs.  No need to sort.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,2)CPT(Wrk_Median,(Wrk_GoodPVs[0]+Wrk_GoodPVs[1])/2.0)JMP(Only2PVs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="64" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an ODD number of good PVs, the median is the central value from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,3)MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[1],Wrk_Median)JMP(DoDeviation);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="65" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an EVEN number of good PVs, the median is the average of the TWO central values
from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4)CPT(Wrk_Median,(Wrk_GoodPVs[1]+Wrk_GoodPVs[2])/2.0)JMP(DoDeviation);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="66" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an ODD number of good PVs, the median is the central value from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,5)MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[2],Wrk_Median)JMP(DoDeviation);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="67" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an EVEN number of good PVs, the median is the average of the TWO central values
from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,6)CPT(Wrk_Median,(Wrk_GoodPVs[2]+Wrk_GoodPVs[3])/2.0)JMP(DoDeviation);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="68" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an ODD number of good PVs, the median is the central value from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,7)MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[3],Wrk_Median)JMP(DoDeviation);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="69" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For an EVEN number of good PVs, the median is the average of the TWO central values
from the sorted set of PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,8)CPT(Wrk_Median,(Wrk_GoodPVs[3]+Wrk_GoodPVs[4])/2.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="70" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute "mean plus 2 SDs" and "mean minus 2 SDs"
for use in checking individual sensors.  (This avoids recomputing these
values in multple CMP instructions, saving scan time.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(DoDeviation)OTU(Wrk_RejectDev)CPT(Wrk_Plus2Std,Wrk_Avg+2.0*Wrk_Std)CPT(Wrk_Minus2Std,Wrk_Avg-2.0*Wrk_Std)CLR(Wrk_WorstDev)CLR(Wrk_WorstPtr);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="71" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV A sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.0)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVA,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVA,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVA-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVA-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVA-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [CLR(Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="72" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV B sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.1)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVB,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVB,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVB-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVB-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVB-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(1,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="73" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV C sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.2)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVC,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVC,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVC-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVC-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVC-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(2,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="74" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV D sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.3)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVD,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVD,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVD-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVD-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVD-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(3,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="75" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV E sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.4)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVE,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVE,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVE-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVE-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVE-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(4,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="76" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV F sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.5)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVF,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVF,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVF-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVF-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVF-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(5,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="77" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV G sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.6)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVG,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVG,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVG-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVG-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVG-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(6,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="78" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[See if the PV H sensor has high deviation.
If selected to use Standard Deviation, and there are at least 4 good PVs,
see if this PV is outside two standard deviations of the mean.
Otherwise, see if this PV is outside the configured absoluted deviation
threshold from the mean.

If the deviation (either way) is high, it is noted that there is at least one rejected PV.
This PV is checked to see if it has the HIGHEST deviation.
Only the highest deviation PV is rejected, then the mean is recalculated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.7)[XIC(Cfg_UseStdDev) GEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) [GRT(Val_PVH,Wrk_Plus2Std) ,LES(Val_PVH,Wrk_Minus2Std) ] ,[XIO(Cfg_UseStdDev) ,LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,4) ] [XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVH-Wrk_Avg)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) CMP(ABS(Val_PVH-Wrk_Median)>=Cfg_AbsDevLim) ] ][OTL(Wrk_RejectDev) CPT(Wrk_Dev,ABS(Val_PVH-Wrk_Avg)) ,GRT(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) [MOV(7,Wrk_WorstPtr) ,MOV(Wrk_Dev,Wrk_WorstDev) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="79" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY sensor was rejected for being outside 2 standard deviations
from the mean, go back and recompute the mean and stadard devaition
of the remaining "good" sensors.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_RejectDev)OTL(Wrk_RejectedPVs.[Wrk_WorstPtr])OTL(Wrk_AnyReject)JMP(Recalc);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="80" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SELECT FINAL MEAN OR MEDIAN
============================================================
If there are NO valid (unrejected) sensors, set the PV to NOT A NUMBER.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Only1PV)EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,0)MOV(16#7F80_0001,Wrk_CalcPVDINT)COP(Wrk_CalcPVDINT,Wrk_PV,1)JMP(SelSubst);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="81" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If there is ONLY ONE valid PV, it is the final value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,1)MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[0],Wrk_PV)JMP(SelSubst);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="82" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Special Case:  If there are exactly two good PVs, select the PV value from
the sorted input list based on the configuration Cfg_CalcWhen2:
0 = select average of the two input,
1 = select minimum (first element in sorted list),
2 = select maximum (second element in sorted list)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Only2PVs)EQU(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,2)[MOV(Wrk_Median,Wrk_PV) ,EQU(Cfg_CalcWhen2,1) MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[0],Wrk_PV) ,EQU(Cfg_CalcWhen2,2) MOV(Wrk_GoodPVs[1],Wrk_PV) ]JMP(SelSubst);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="83" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If there are THREE OR MORE valid PVs, use the already-computed
average or median of the good PVs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_CalcAvg) MOV(Wrk_Avg,Wrk_PV) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcAvg) MOV(Wrk_Median,Wrk_PV) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="84" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SELECT NORMAL OR SUBSTITUTE PV
============================================================
The Value shows the selected PV.
With Substitute PV enabled, it's the value of the entered MSet_SubstPV.
In normal operation, it's the value (Wrk_PV) selected above: the
Min, Max, Average or selected scaled Input (Inp_PVA, Inp_PVB)
 or Simulatied PV (Set_SimPVA, Set_SimPVB).

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SelSubst)[XIO(Sts_SubstPV) COP(Wrk_PV,Wrk_UnfiltPV,1) ,XIC(Wrk_SubstPV) COP(MSet_SubstPV,Wrk_UnfiltPV,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="85" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PV FIRST-ORDER FILTER PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung determines whether the Analog PV (unfiltered) is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber.
In either case, the value cannot be passed into the filter calculation.  Instead, it is
just copied to the PV directly.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Wrk_UnfiltPV,Wrk_CalcPVDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_CalcPVDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_CalcPVInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="86" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If tracking is enabled and the Untiltered PV is NOT Infinite or NaN,
copy it to the Substitute PV Setting.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_SetTrack)COP(Wrk_UnfiltPV,MSet_SubstPV,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="87" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[In preparation for calculating the Filtered PV, this rung
determines the time since the previous scan, using a non-stop TON timer.
When we get here, we read the accumulator (in milliseconds, so
divide by 1000.0 to get seconds), then clear the accumulator.  Next scan the accumulator will have
incremented up to the number of milliseconds since last scan.  (Works for scan times up to 2 million seconds.....)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(2147483647,Wrk_ScanT.PRE)TON(Wrk_ScanT,?,?)DIV(Wrk_ScanT.ACC,1000.0,Wrk_ScanTime)CLR(Wrk_ScanT.ACC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="88" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the input was +/-Infinity or Not a Number and it becomes a valid number,
initialize the filter to start from the first valid value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_CalcPVInfNaN)ONS(Wrk_ValidONS)MOV(Wrk_UnfiltPV,Wrk_FiltPV);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="89" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Calculate the FILTERED PV. 
First, calculate "alpha", the portion of the difference between input and previous value to move toward the input.
Then calculate the new value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Cfg_FiltTC,0.0) CPT(Wrk_Alpha,1.0/(1.0+Wrk_ScanTime/Cfg_FiltTC)) ,LEQ(Cfg_FiltTC,0.0) CLR(Wrk_Alpha) ,XIO(Wrk_CalcPVInfNaN) CPT(Wrk_FiltPV,(Wrk_Alpha*Wrk_FiltPV)+((1.0-Wrk_Alpha)*Wrk_UnfiltPV)) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="90" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Filtered PV becomes the final Value (Val) for the Analog Input block.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_CalcPVInfNaN) MOV(Wrk_FiltPV,Val) ,XIC(Wrk_CalcPVInfNaN) COP(Wrk_UnfiltPV,Val,1) ,COP(Wrk_PV,Val_CalcPV,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="91" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CAPTURE MIN / MAX PV EXCURSION
============================================================
Capture the PV Maximum Excursion (highest value reached) and
PV Minimum Excursion (lowest value reached) since last cleared.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_CalcPVInfNaN)[GRT(Val,Val_PVMaxCapt) MOV(Val,Val_PVMaxCapt) ,LES(Val,Val_PVMinCapt) MOV(Val,Val_PVMinCapt) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="92" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CLEAR CAPTURED MIN / MAX COMMAND PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung "clears" the captured Minimum and Maximum
by setting them to the current PV Value.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_ClearCapt) OTU(OCmd_ClearCapt) ,XIC(PCmd_ClearCapt) OTU(PCmd_ClearCapt) ]XIO(Wrk_CalcPVInfNaN)MOV(Val,Val_PVMaxCapt)MOV(Val,Val_PVMinCapt);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="93" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ANALOG THRESHOLD STATUS PROCESSING
============================================================
If the Analog Value is Infinite or Not a Number, skip the compares
to avoid Minor Faults and just flag the value as Bad below.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_CalcPVInfNaN)OTU(Wrk_HiHi)OTU(Wrk_Hi)OTU(Wrk_Lo)OTU(Wrk_LoLo)JMP(Alarms);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="94" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Analog Value exceeds the High-High limit for the On-Delay Time,
issue the PV High-High Status.
If the Analog Value falls back below the limit (minus deadband) for the
Off-Delay Time, clear the PV High-High Status.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GEQ(Val,Val_HiHiLim) OTL(Wrk_HiHi) ,CMP(Val<(Val_HiHiLim-Cfg_HiHiDB)) OTU(Wrk_HiHi) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="95" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Analog Value exceeds the High limit for the On-Delay Time,
issue the PV High Status.
If the Analog Value falls back below the limit (minus deadband) for the
Off-Delay Time, clear the PV High Status.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GEQ(Val,Val_HiLim) OTL(Wrk_Hi) ,CMP(Val<(Val_HiLim-Cfg_HiDB)) OTU(Wrk_Hi) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="96" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Analog Value falls below the Low limit for the On-Delay Time,
issue the PV Low Status.
If the Analog Value rises back above the limit (plus deadband) for the
Off-Delay Time, clear the PV Low Status.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LEQ(Val,Val_LoLim) OTL(Wrk_Lo) ,CMP(Val>(Val_LoLim+Cfg_LoDB)) OTU(Wrk_Lo) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="97" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Analog Value falls below the Low-Low limit for the On-Delay Time,
issue the PV Low-Low Status.
If the Analog Value rises back above the limit (plus deadband) for the
Off-Delay Time, clear the PV Low-Low Status.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LEQ(Val,Val_LoLoLim) OTL(Wrk_LoLo) ,CMP(Val>(Val_LoLoLim+Cfg_LoLoDB)) OTU(Wrk_LoLo) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="98" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
If the Analog Value exceeds the High-High limit for the On-Delay Time,
issue the PV High-High Status.
If the Analog Value falls back below the limit (minus deadband) for the
Off-Delay Time, clear the PV High-High Status.

#####  V3.0-00 2013-10-30:  Modified rung to use P_Gate.  #####
#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Alarms)[XIC(Wrk_HiHi) OTE(Sts_HiHiCmp) ,P_Gate(HiHiGate) ,XIC(HiHiGate.Out) OTE(Sts_HiHi) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="99" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Analog Value exceeds the High limit for the On-Delay Time,
issue the PV High Status.
If the Analog Value falls back below the limit (minus deadband) for the
Off-Delay Time, clear the PV High Status.

#####  V3.0-00 2013-10-30:  Modified rung to use P_Gate.  #####
#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Hi) OTE(Sts_HiCmp) ,P_Gate(HiGate) ,XIC(HiGate.Out) OTE(Sts_Hi) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="100" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Analog Value falls below the Low limit for the On-Delay Time,
issue the PV Low Status.
If the Analog Value rises back above the limit (plus deadband) for the
Off-Delay Time, clear the PV Low Status.

#####  V3.0-00 2013-10-30:  Modified rung to use P_Gate.  #####
#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Lo) OTE(Sts_LoCmp) ,P_Gate(LoGate) ,XIC(LoGate.Out) OTE(Sts_Lo) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="101" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Analog Value falls below the Low-Low limit for the On-Delay Time,
issue the PV Low-Low Status.
If the Analog Value rises back above the limit (plus deadband) for the
Off-Delay Time, clear the PV Low-Low Status.

#####  V3.0-00 2013-10-30:  Modified rung to use P_Gate.  #####
#####  V3.0-04  2014-04-04:  Modified to better handle Inf/NaN to avoid Minor Faults.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_LoLo) OTE(Sts_LoLoCmp) ,P_Gate(LoLoGate) ,XIC(LoLoGate.Out) OTE(Sts_LoLo) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="102" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ANALOG QUALITY / STATUS PROCESSING
============================================================
If any PV that's enabled has been rejected for any reason,
flag that PV with a Rejected Status bit.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_UsePVA) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.0) OTE(Sts_PVAReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVB) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.1) OTE(Sts_PVBReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVC) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.2) OTE(Sts_PVCReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVD) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.3) OTE(Sts_PVDReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVE) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.4) OTE(Sts_PVEReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVF) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.5) OTE(Sts_PVFReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVG) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.6) OTE(Sts_PVGReject) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePVH) XIC(Wrk_RejectedPVs.7) OTE(Sts_PVHReject) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="103" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[A summary Status bit is set if ANY PV is rejected.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_AnyReject)OTE(Sts_AnyReject);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="104" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If we have rejected PVs and this results in having only the minimum required
number of good PVs, set a warning Status bit.  The meaning of this Status is
basically that the next PV to be rejected will result in a BAD PV (fail).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Cfg_MinGood)XIC(Sts_AnyReject)OTE(Sts_MinGood);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="105" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Analog Value rises above the Fail High Limit or falls below the
Fail Low Limit for the On-Delay Time, or if the Bad PV Input is
asserted and the input is not in Simulation, raise a PV Fail Status.

If the Analog Value is back in range, that is, it is below the Fail High Limit (minus
deadband) and above the Fail Low Limit (plus deadband), for the Off-Delay Time,
AND if the Bad PV input clears or the input is Siimulated,
clear the PV Fail Status.

@@@@@  NOTE:  The GEQ and LEQ take care of +/- Inf and +/- NaN for us automatically!  @@@@@

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Modified rung to use P_Gate.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Wrk_NumGoodPVs,Cfg_MinGood) OTE(Sts_FailCmp) ,P_Gate(FailGate) ,[XIC(FailGate.Out) XIO(Wrk_SubstPV) ,XIC(Wrk_CalcPVInfNaN) ,XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ] OTE(Sts_Fail) OTE(Sts_PVBad) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="106" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If any of the NON-REJECTED inputs (used in the calculation of the PV)
is UNCERTAIN, the calculated PV is Uncertain.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_PVAUncertain) XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.0) ,XIC(Inp_PVBUncertain) XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.1) ,XIC(Inp_PVCUncertain) XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.2) ,XIC(Inp_PVDUncertain) XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.3) ,XIC(Inp_PVEUncertain) XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.4) ,XIC(Inp_PVFUncertain) XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.5) ,XIC(Inp_PVGUncertain) XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.6) ,XIC(Inp_PVHUncertain) XIO(Wrk_RejectedPVs.7) ]OTE(Sts_PVUncertain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="107" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Flag a Configuration Error if any Status On-Delay, Off-Delay
or Gate Delay timer preset is invalid
(and set timer to a default, non-faulting value).

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Modified rung to add gate delays.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(HiHiGate.Sts_Err) ,XIC(HiGate.Sts_Err) ,XIC(LoGate.Sts_Err) ,XIC(LoLoGate.Sts_Err) ,XIC(FailGate.Sts_Err) ]OTE(Err_Timer);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="108" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles the reports of all Bad Configuration Status.
Individual bits are provided for various status:
Bad Raw Scaling configs
Bad Engineering Units Scaling configs
Bad 1st-Order Filter configs
Bad Alarm Deadband configs
Bad Alarm Minimum Duration configs
Bad Cfg_HasPVx configs (at least one must be set)
Bad Cfg_UsePVx configs (at least one must be set)

Then a summary Bad Config status is provided, simply an OR of the individual bits.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ,XIC(Err_Filt) ,XIC(Err_MinGood) ,XIC(Err_Timer) ,[LES(Cfg_HiHiDB,0.0) ,LES(Cfg_HiDB,0.0) ,LES(Cfg_LoDB,0.0) ,LES(Cfg_LoLoDB,0.0) ,LES(Cfg_FailDB,0.0) ] OTE(Err_DB) ,EQU(Wrk_NumInputs,0) OTE(Err_Has) ,XIO(Err_Has) XIO(Cfg_UsePVA) XIO(Cfg_UsePVB) XIO(Cfg_UsePVC) XIO(Cfg_UsePVD) XIO(Cfg_UsePVE) XIO(Cfg_UsePVF) XIO(Cfg_UsePVG) XIO(Cfg_UsePVH) OTE(Err_Use) ,[XIC(HiHi.Sts_Err) ,XIC(Hi.Sts_Err) ,XIC(Lo.Sts_Err) ,XIC(LoLo.Sts_Err) ,XIC(AnyReject.Sts_Err) ,XIC(MinGood.Sts_Err) ,XIC(Fail.Sts_Err) ] OTE(Err_Alarm) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="109" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED STATUS VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_PVA
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasChanObjA) MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQA) ,XIC(Cfg_HasChanObjA) MOV(Inp_PVASrcQ,Wrk_SrcQA) ,XIC(Inp_PVAUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQA) ,XIC(Inp_PVABad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQA) ,[XIC(Wrk_InpAInfNaN) ,XIC(Wrk_PVAOutOfRange) ] MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQA) ,[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ] MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQA) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQA) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQA,SrcQ_IOA) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="110" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_PVB
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasChanObjB) MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQB) ,XIC(Cfg_HasChanObjB) MOV(Inp_PVBSrcQ,Wrk_SrcQB) ,XIC(Inp_PVBUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQB) ,XIC(Inp_PVBBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQB) ,[XIC(Wrk_InpBInfNaN) ,XIC(Wrk_PVBOutOfRange) ] MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQB) ,[XIC(Err_Raw) ,XIC(Err_EU) ] MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQB) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQB) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQB,SrcQ_IOB) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
